---
import ManPageLayout from '../../layouts/ManPageLayout.astro';
const links = [
  { id: 'name', label: 'NAME' },
  { id: 'principles', label: 'PRINCIPLES' },
  { id: 'software', label: 'SOFTWARE' },
  { id: 'revision', label: 'REVISION' },
  { id: 'also', label: 'SEE ALSO' }
];
---

<ManPageLayout
  title="Philosophy"
  description="Working principles about software, simplicity, ownership, and changing one's mind."
  manual="PHILOSOPHY(7)"
  links={links}
>
  <section id="name" class="man-section">
    <h2>NAME</h2>
    <h1>
      Philosophy <small>Working beliefs, not commandments.</small>
    </h1>
  </section>
  <section id="principles" class="man-section">
    <h2>PRINCIPLES</h2>
    <dl class="definition-list">
      <dt>understand first</dt>
      <dd>
        Abstraction is useful after the underlying problem is understood, not as a substitute for
        understanding it.
      </dd>
      <dt>complexity costs</dt>
      <dd>
        A complicated system needs to earn its complexity. “Enterprise” and “modern” are not reasons
        by themselves.
      </dd>
      <dt>users matter</dt>
      <dd>
        Tools should respect the person running them: their privacy, agency, data, attention, and
        ability to leave.
      </dd>
      <dt>specific beats grand</dt>
      <dd>
        A small tool that solves one real problem is often more valuable than a broad promise.
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section id="software" class="man-section">
    <h2>SOFTWARE</h2>
    <p class="lede">I prefer software I can inspect, adapt, keep, and share.</p>
    <p>
      Free and open-source software is not automatically good software, but it preserves
      possibilities that closed systems remove. It lets curiosity continue past the interface and
      gives users a meaningful form of ownership.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="revision" class="man-section">
    <h2>REVISION</h2>
    <p>
      These views are expected to change. A belief that cannot survive better evidence is not a
      principle; it is an attachment.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="also" class="man-section">
    <h2>SEE ALSO</h2>
    <div class="see-also">
      <a href="/about/">about(7)</a>
      <a href="/uses/">uses(7)</a>
      <a href="/writing/">writing(5)</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</ManPageLayout>
